# Deploy to Fly after commit and push

Production is https://nwtracker.fly.dev/ (`fly` app `nwtracker`, region `lhr`). A git push does not update that host by itself.

Whenever you create a git commit and push it to origin:

1. Immediately run `fly deploy -a nwtracker` from the repo root. Do not wait to be asked.
2. Wait until the deploy finishes. Confirm with `fly status -a nwtracker` that a new image is live.
3. If deploy fails (Dockerfile, migrations, health checks), fix it and deploy again.

GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/fly-deploy.yml`) also deploys on push to `main`. Still run `fly deploy` from this session after you push, unless a deploy for the same commit is already in progress.

Never commit Fly tokens, `.env`, or GitHub secrets.
